(Regression test: an out-of-bounds list access sets _last_error, but a later
successful list access clears it so a subsequent On error does not fire.)

A list called nums is [10, 20, 30].
A number called bad is element 100 of nums.
On error print "first".

A number called bad2 is element 200 of nums.
A number called good is element 1 of nums.
On error print "second".
